# UI components (`@stream-kit/ui`)

Before building custom markup for common UI patterns, check whether `@stream-kit/ui` already provides a component. Browse `packages/ui/src/lib/components/` or import from the package subpaths in `packages/ui/package.json`.

## Available components

| Import | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `@stream-kit/ui/alert` | Info, success, warning, and error callouts |
| `@stream-kit/ui/badge` | Status labels and counts |
| `@stream-kit/ui/blueprint` | Marketing/dashboard schematic chrome (GridFrame, SectionRule, Crosshair, CellGrid, Panel, Eyebrow) |
| `@stream-kit/ui/button` | Actions and icon buttons |
| `@stream-kit/ui/container` | Page width constraints |
| `@stream-kit/ui/data-table` | Presentational data tables (columns, sticky header, scroll, empty state) |
| `@stream-kit/ui/dialog` | Low-level dialog primitives (prefer `app.createModal` in the app layer) |
| `@stream-kit/ui/dropdown` | Menus and action lists |
| `@stream-kit/ui/empty-state` | Full-area list empty states (icon, title, description, CTA) |
| `@stream-kit/ui/heading` | Section titles |
| `@stream-kit/ui/input` | Text, select, checkbox, switch, slider, file, one-of inputs |
| `@stream-kit/ui/popover` | Anchored popovers |
| `@stream-kit/ui/scroll-area` | Scrollable regions |
| `@stream-kit/ui/toggle-group` | Mutually exclusive option toggles (choose A/B, view/edit) |
| `@stream-kit/ui/tooltip` | Hover/focus hints |

See also `@stream-kit/ui/blocks` for declarative page blocks (settings, alerts, etc.).

## Examples

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Custom alert markup -->
<div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 px-4 py-3">
  <Icon icon="ri:information-line" />
  <p>{message}</p>
</div>

<!-- ✅ Alert component -->
<Alert icon="ri:sparkling-2-line" description={message} />
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ Raw <button> for primary actions -->
<button class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2">Save</button>

<!-- ✅ Button component -->
<Button icon="ri:save-line" onclick={save}>Save</Button>
```

## App-layer exceptions

- **Modals** → `app.createModal` (see `modals.mdc`), not `@stream-kit/ui/dialog` directly.
- **Confirmations** → `app.confirm.ask()`, not a custom dialog.
- **Domain-specific layouts** (dashboard grid, stat cards) may stay custom when no UI component fits.

## When adding new UI

If a pattern is reused in multiple places and no UI component exists yet, consider adding it to `packages/ui` instead of copying styles across the app.
